A||||13||saleenfiero||What would it take to beat a '92 mustang GT auto?||||1||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||05-25-2001||12:28 PM||||I know, I know, a 3.4.  But other than that, how do the auto GT's launch?  I've heard that they kind of suck.  So what could I do to my stocker 2.8 to have a chance?  Oh yeah, I'm handicapped with an automatic too.||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||05-25-2001||12:32 PM||||humm not good my man, maybe a steam catapult would do the trick but you need an aircraft carier for that.||||reg||6
Z||000002||fyerstarter||05-25-2001||12:37 PM||||Auto's suck! I just bought a new 87 GT auto completely stock with only 10k miles on a rebuilt motor and that thing is a dog like I cannot believe. My other car a 87 GT stick with a few mods (intake, headers, 3 angle valve job, msd ignition, accell module, under-drive pulleys) will smoke the ****  out of that thing. I know it has a few mods but they should not account for that big of a difference in my mind. Maybe 10 hp at the wheels if I'm lucky. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||05-25-2001||01:48 PM||||Agreed, I had the same issues with my auto....  from a stop it's a dog, once I am rolling LOOK OUT!  BanditBalz beats me off the line NO PROBLEMS in his 2.8 Stick, my 2.8 auto lags back but he doesn't gain TOO much ground ahead of me... I am running a 2.8 crane cam and I changed my Torque Converter to a higher stall, THAT'S my reccomendation, change your Torque converter, it made a HUGE Difference in my car, night and day!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||05-25-2001||02:14 PM||||<P>You have to build a high power motor to run fast with an auto. There is a guy in Toronto who has a built up 3.1ltr motor , with all sorts of mods , it runs high 15's. HEre is a run down of what is in his motor according to the display by his car.<P>3.1ltr engine<BR>Crame cam<BR>1.6 rockers<BR>10:1 compression<BR>port and polished heads<BR>crane valve springs<BR>balanced and blueprinted<BR>3800 Tq converter<BR>MSD Hi 6<BR>cold air induction<P>Autos' have 3.35(?) gear ratio's. Hook up a 4 speed muncie to the above setup and I bet it's a high 14 sec car. 4spds have 3.65 rear gears , 60mph 2nd gear depending on tire size and most people never take a 4spd out of 3rd gear at the strip. <P>If you want to put a scare into 5.0ltrs , save the Tq converter and buy a NOS kit , Shaun41178 on the forum has a auto with a few light mods running NOS nearly into the 13's, I believe his setup has been fairly trouble free too. Thats with a STOCK Auto Tranny!!!<P>The 4spd's 3.65 ratio takes better advantage of the engines power curve. Autos'a are great when they have the torque to back up the auto tranny. If you want to skip the NOS I would talk to archie about who he gets to build Auto Tranny's. I know in most cases he uses a stock tranny , but I'm sure he knows lots of tricks , or can direct you as to where you can get some performance out of your auto tranny.<P>personally for the cost of pulling a tranny and putting in a new TQ converter , I would go with the NOS. you can use it when you want , the 3800TQ converter will suck gas all the time , more permanent.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.<P>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-25-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||05-25-2001||03:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B>What would it take to beat a '92 mustang GT auto?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Answer: A 4 year old on a Big Wheel.<P>Did I win?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||sluppy123||05-25-2001||05:21 PM||||My 87 GT with auto tranny launches very hard, I know I could take a GT stang if it was stock,{i've stayed with a 98? cobra up to 70mph) but I would have to use the funny gas. I have a B&M shift kit installed, When I'm on nitrous it chirps the tires shifting from 1st to second, with zero wheel spin at launch. <BR>Throw some curves in that race and see what happens.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Eibach springs, RSM side scoops, Mr Mikes leather, 70hp NOS, 17" Mille Miglia's, and lots more.<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=12781563&p=48213929&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
