Z||000013||Formula88||05-26-2001||08:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>How about an 87 Grand National? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Geez, how about a wild card here!  Are we talking a stock 87 GN?  Ok, then you'll need to run low-14's to maybe high 13's.  Um, now FIND a stock 87 GN.  Most are running in the 12s at least, possibly faster.  <P>When I had my 87 GN, all I did was put in a 160* thermostat and Kenne-Belle Hi-Lo Pro chip and WATCH OUT!  That beast was running 19psi boost (13-14 was stock).  It was hard to launch, cuz without enough boost, you bog - too much and you blow away the tires, but nothing, I mean NOTHING could ever beat me off the line if I didn't screw up.  I'm not saying there weren't faster cars out there, but in 3 years of looking, I never found one.  That included late 80 and early 90s Muscrats with NOS!  It was almost as fast as the 72 455HO Trans Am I had when I was in college.  <P>And still, I have to say my 88 Formula is more fun than either car.  It's close between the Fiero and the TA, cuz man I love my big blocks, but the Fiero is soooo much fun - albeit not anywhere near as fast.  I guess I'll have to wait till I do an engine swap so I can have the best of both worlds in the Fiero.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If I can beat a new z28, Muscrat or Vette, I'm happy.  I'll take 'em on in handling right now, but need a bit more power for the straight line.  Won't stop me from trying, though.  So much comes down to driver skill....||||reg||1
